2
00:00:28.820 --> 00:00:31.406
<i>Some people are born winners.</i>

3
00:00:32.031 --> 00:00:33.824
<i>Tom Brady.</i>

4
00:00:33.825 --> 00:00:35.284
<i>LeBron James.</i>

5
00:00:35.285 --> 00:00:36.994
{\an8}<i>Joey Chestnut</i>

6
00:00:36.995 --> 00:00:39.206
{\an8}<i>and also me.</i>

7
00:00:40.624 --> 00:00:42.667
<i>My name is Dusty Boyd.</i>

8
00:00:42.668 --> 00:00:45.796
<i>but most people on planet Earth
know me as The Hammer.</i>

9
00:00:46.296 --> 00:00:49.465
<i>My dad gave me that nickname
before he even told me my real name.</i>

10
00:00:49.466 --> 00:00:51.384
Yeah. that's the way to go. Hammer. Yeah.

11
00:00:51.385 --> 00:00:54.470
<i>And he trained me like a tennis racehorse.</i>

12
00:00:54.471 --> 00:00:58.475
<i>Cardio. strength training.
taping tennis rackets to my hands.</i>

13
00:00:59.142 --> 00:01:01.394
<i>My dad wasn't like other dads.</i>

14
00:01:01.395 --> 00:01:04.815
<i>He didn't teach me how to read.
He taught me how to hit.</i>

15
00:01:05.440 --> 00:01:06.607
We're on our way. Hammer!

16
00:01:06.608 --> 00:01:10.862
{\an8}<i>And it worked.
I broke every single USTA junior record.</i>

17
00:01:10.863 --> 00:01:15.449
<i>Wins. aces. shutouts.
You name it. they were mine.</i>

18
00:01:15.450 --> 00:01:17.702
<i>And soon the world took notice.</i>

19
00:01:17.703 --> 00:01:19.787
No. Dave. I don't hit hard.

20
00:01:19.788 --> 00:01:21.248
I hit the hardest.

21
00:01:23.709 --> 00:01:25.961
<i>And before I even graduated high school.</i>

22
00:01:26.879 --> 00:01:29.964
- <i>I lived out me and my dad's dream.</i>
- Dusty. over here!

23
00:01:29.965 --> 00:01:33.176
- <i>I turned pro.</i>
- Right here! Dusty. over here!

24
00:01:33.177 --> 00:01:37.014
<i>And that. my friends.
is my incredible true story.</i>

25
00:01:39.099 --> 00:01:42.226
So. does anybody have any questions?

26
00:01:42.227 --> 00:01:44.353
Yeah. are we ever gonna
hit a fucking ball?

27
00:01:44.354 --> 00:01:45.938
This lesson sucks ass.

28
00:01:45.939 --> 00:01:49.734
I meant does anybody have any questions
about the story that I was just telling?

29
00:01:49.735 --> 00:01:51.235
And that was very clear. wasn't it?

30
00:01:51.236 --> 00:01:53.988
Very clear story.
And I've actually got a question. King.

31
00:01:53.989 --> 00:01:55.990
This is what I was looking for.
PJ. go ahead.

32
00:01:55.991 --> 00:01:59.911
Why does it still give me chills
every damn time I hear it?

33
00:01:59.912 --> 00:02:01.662
- Gives me chills too.
- Seriously. I think. like.

34
00:02:01.663 --> 00:02:03.456
- you're one of the best--
- If you're so good.

35
00:02:03.457 --> 00:02:05.917
how come you work for your dad
teaching nine-year-olds?

36
00:02:05.918 --> 00:02:09.169
I think these punks need to hear
the Andy Roddick story.

37
00:02:09.170 --> 00:02:11.088
- Oh. you do. do you?
- Oh. no. no. no. no.

38
00:02:11.089 --> 00:02:12.965
- Please don't tell another story.
- Vero Beach Classic.

39
00:02:12.966 --> 00:02:14.050
Oh. my God!

40
00:02:14.051 --> 00:02:16.720
The year was 2000. Me versus Andy Roddick.

41
00:02:17.846 --> 00:02:21.682
<i>He was technically the bigger name.
but everybody was there to see me.</i>

42
00:02:21.683 --> 00:02:23.726
{\an8}Love you. Hammer!

43
00:02:23.727 --> 00:02:25.728
{\an8}<i>We'd played a couple times as amateurs.</i>

44
00:02:25.729 --> 00:02:29.065
And every time I saw him.
I used to cream his ass.

45
00:02:29.066 --> 00:02:30.274
No other way to say it.

46
00:02:30.275 --> 00:02:31.443
Pretty sure there is.

47
00:02:32.819 --> 00:02:36.198
<i>But this was the first time
meeting as professionals.</i>

48
00:02:40.369 --> 00:02:42.538
- <i>And I was crushing him.</i>
- Yes.

49
00:02:43.872 --> 00:02:45.414
Way to go. Hammer.

50
00:02:45.415 --> 00:02:46.958
That's my son.

51
00:02:46.959 --> 00:02:51.963
<i>That's where evil Mr. Andy
decided to play dirty.</i>

52
00:02:51.964 --> 00:02:55.007
<i>Yeah. He tried to ice me
by taking a bathroom break.</i>

53
00:02:55.008 --> 00:02:56.718
<i>So I ran down there to confront him.</i>

54
00:02:57.845 --> 00:02:59.721
<i>Slipped on a wet spot.</i>

55
00:03:00.764 --> 00:03:03.100
- <i>And shattered my wrist.</i>
- Ow!

56
00:03:03.767 --> 00:03:05.644
Roddick!

57
00:03:06.228 --> 00:03:11.190
And in doing so.
I shattered my very promising career.

58
00:03:11.191 --> 00:03:13.693
- What?
- Obviously. Andy Frauddick.

59
00:03:13.694 --> 00:03:16.195
he'd slicked down the floor
with some type of substance.

60
00:03:16.196 --> 00:03:19.490
And that means that all of
Roddick's professional achievements.

61
00:03:19.491 --> 00:03:23.160
like winning the US Open
and marrying supermodel Brooklyn Decker.

62
00:03:23.161 --> 00:03:24.829
those are all actually Dusty's.

63
00:03:24.830 --> 00:03:26.247
That's actually a really interesting idea.

64
00:03:26.248 --> 00:03:27.707
- I'd never thought of that. I guess--
- I'm sorry.

65
00:03:27.708 --> 00:03:30.126
How does that make
his accomplishments yours again?

66
00:03:30.127 --> 00:03:32.211
Yeah. I'm struggling to
connect those dots as well.

67
00:03:32.212 --> 00:03:34.715
Well. maybe you need to go
to dot-connecting lessons.

68
00:03:35.799 --> 00:03:36.924
Nice burn.

69
00:03:36.925 --> 00:03:39.427
Anyway. I'm done talking to you guys.
I've gotten very bored.

70
00:03:39.428 --> 00:03:41.095
I don't think you're gonna
learn the lessons.

71
00:03:41.096 --> 00:03:42.597
So you guys wanna
hit some tennis balls or what?

72
00:03:42.598 --> 00:03:45.559
- Yes. Finally. Oh. my God! Please.
- Yes. Please.

73
00:03:53.567 --> 00:03:54.568
One second.

74
00:03:55.235 --> 00:03:56.652
Something I need to do.

75
00:03:56.653 --> 00:03:58.529
- Hey!
- Sorry about that.

76
00:03:58.530 --> 00:04:00.031
- Little help?
- Yeah. My pleasure.

77
00:04:00.032 --> 00:04:01.116
Here's your pickleball.

78
00:04:02.159 --> 00:04:03.410
In the garbage!

79
00:04:03.994 --> 00:04:05.579
This is a tennis club. lady.

80
00:04:06.079 --> 00:04:07.873
- Asshole!
- I heard that.

81
00:04:08.498 --> 00:04:11.834
Good. I wanted you to.
That's why I said it so loudly.

82
00:04:11.835 --> 00:04:13.920
Okay. pickleball lady. Let's do this.

83
00:04:13.921 --> 00:04:15.588
Peej. I have a game.

84
00:04:15.589 --> 00:04:17.088
You like games.
You play pickleball. right?

85
00:04:17.089 --> 00:04:18.758
- See this quarter?
- Yes.

86
00:04:18.759 --> 00:04:22.387
Place it anywhere you want on the court
and I got one shot to hit it.

87
00:04:22.930 --> 00:04:25.681
If I hit it. you're banned for life.

88
00:04:25.682 --> 00:04:29.936
And if I miss. I will waive
your membership fees for a year.

89
00:04:29.937 --> 00:04:31.354
Oh. I'm banned?

90
00:04:31.355 --> 00:04:33.564
Well. it doesn't matter
because I'm not a member here.

91
00:04:33.565 --> 00:04:34.941
I'm just taking a lesson.

92
00:04:34.942 --> 00:04:36.693
So let's do this. I'll sweeten the deal.

93
00:04:37.194 --> 00:04:38.612
If I miss this shot.

94
00:04:39.530 --> 00:04:40.780
I'll toss in these.

95
00:04:40.781 --> 00:04:43.699
Dusty. no. Not your 1999 Buick LeSabre?

96
00:04:43.700 --> 00:04:49.705
Yes. I will toss in my 1999 Buick LeSabre
with under 200.000 miles on it.

97
00:04:49.706 --> 00:04:51.083
Now I'm torn.

98
00:04:52.251 --> 00:04:55.963
Don't really wanna talk to you anymore.
but I do wanna see if you can hit it.

99
00:04:57.297 --> 00:04:58.923
What to do? Okay.

100
00:04:58.924 --> 00:04:59.925
Let's play.

101
00:05:01.718 --> 00:05:02.927
Anywhere?

102
00:05:02.928 --> 00:05:04.011
Anywhere you want.

103
00:05:04.012 --> 00:05:07.056
I choose there.

104
00:05:07.057 --> 00:05:09.226
Tricky. In the corner.

105
00:05:22.030 --> 00:05:23.322
Yes!

106
00:05:23.323 --> 00:05:25.826
Get out! Get out! Get out!

107
00:05:29.329 --> 00:05:30.413
Jesus.

108
00:05:30.414 --> 00:05:31.998
Get your pickleball ass out of here.

109
00:05:31.999 --> 00:05:33.000
Before you go.

110
00:05:33.750 --> 00:05:35.627
Smile. you're banned.

111
00:05:37.504 --> 00:05:39.547
Whatever. Man.

112
00:05:39.548 --> 00:05:41.133
Yeah!

113
00:05:44.928 --> 00:05:47.805
Can you read what it says
on my nameplate. Dusty?

114
00:05:47.806 --> 00:05:48.890
Of course I can. Dad.

115
00:05:48.891 --> 00:05:52.185
It says. "Chuck Boyd.
President of Tennis Operations."

116
00:05:52.186 --> 00:05:53.604
Holy shit.

117
00:05:54.104 --> 00:05:57.023
- Sounds like a pretty important guy. huh?
- Yeah.

118
00:05:57.024 --> 00:06:00.568
Not that type who'd wanna see his son
dressing like a slob. showing up late.

119
00:06:00.569 --> 00:06:02.653
- banning people from the club.
- Right.

120
00:06:02.654 --> 00:06:04.530
You know. the truth is it's not just you.

121
00:06:04.531 --> 00:06:07.700
This whole club's heading down a bad path
and I'm about to right the ship.

122
00:06:07.701 --> 00:06:12.205
I'm hosting a dinner tonight
for all the top brass and you as well.

123
00:06:12.206 --> 00:06:13.372
Top brass and I'll be there.

124
00:06:13.373 --> 00:06:15.625
Damn right. you will.
And you will not embarrass me.

125
00:06:15.626 --> 00:06:18.211
You will show up on time.
you won't wear some stupid headband.

126
00:06:18.212 --> 00:06:20.296
and you'll bring a plus-one
to show these people

127
00:06:20.297 --> 00:06:22.507
I did not raise
some kind of hopeless loser.

128
00:06:22.508 --> 00:06:23.509
Yes. sir.

129
00:06:24.218 --> 00:06:25.427
You free tonight. my man?

130
00:06:25.969 --> 00:06:27.261
Let me think about that.

131
00:06:27.262 --> 00:06:28.721
Not him!

132
00:06:28.722 --> 00:06:31.141
Bring that girl you've been seeing.
You know. the pretty one.

133
00:06:31.725 --> 00:06:34.018
Unfortunately. Marisa and I… We broke up.

134
00:06:34.019 --> 00:06:36.604
Well. go over and apologize
and get her back.

135
00:06:36.605 --> 00:06:38.397
- It's complicated.
- Go.

136
00:06:38.398 --> 00:06:41.317
Okay. I feel like we spent this whole time
talking about me.

137
00:06:41.318 --> 00:06:42.319
How are you doing?

138
00:06:43.946 --> 00:06:46.198
I'm gonna get going.
I'm gonna go do what you asked me to do.

139
00:06:58.836 --> 00:07:00.170
Come on. You got it.

140
00:07:03.131 --> 00:07:04.715
Well. well. well.

141
00:07:04.716 --> 00:07:07.510
Look who came crawling back
like I knew he would.

142
00:07:07.511 --> 00:07:09.679
- Nope. Changed my mind. Not doing this.
- Wait!

143
00:07:09.680 --> 00:07:11.848
- No. I can't do this. Marisa.
- Yes. you can.

144
00:07:11.849 --> 00:07:13.433
- No. I actually can't.
- Come back.

145
00:07:14.101 --> 00:07:15.518
What do you want?

146
00:07:15.519 --> 00:07:17.103
- I need a favor.
- Okay.

147
00:07:17.104 --> 00:07:19.397
I need you to pretend
we're back together for one night

148
00:07:19.398 --> 00:07:20.815
and come to a dinner at my dad's house.

149
00:07:20.816 --> 00:07:21.899
Oh. my God!

150
00:07:21.900 --> 00:07:24.443
You boys love
your little games. don't you?

151
00:07:24.444 --> 00:07:27.697
One minute. I'm the worst person ever.
You never wanna see me again.

152
00:07:27.698 --> 00:07:29.907
I believe you even called me "unfaithful."

153
00:07:29.908 --> 00:07:33.077
I called you that. Marisa.
because you cheated on me.

154
00:07:33.078 --> 00:07:34.495
Dusty?

155
00:07:34.496 --> 00:07:36.163
- What?
- It was one time.

156
00:07:36.164 --> 00:07:37.206
It was eight times.

157
00:07:37.207 --> 00:07:38.958
Yeah. but it was with one guy.

158
00:07:38.959 --> 00:07:40.418
It was with nine guys!

159
00:07:40.419 --> 00:07:41.878
Oh. my God.

160
00:07:41.879 --> 00:07:43.796
What. are you <i>Rain Man</i>?
You remember everything.

161
00:07:43.797 --> 00:07:46.592
Look. Marisa.
will you please just do me this favor?

162
00:07:47.509 --> 00:07:49.093
- Please.
- Okay. fine.

163
00:07:49.094 --> 00:07:50.136
Thank you.

164
00:07:50.137 --> 00:07:51.762
Yeah. it's so true.

165
00:07:51.763 --> 00:07:54.932
Have you read anything
by that author Malcolm Gladwell?

166
00:07:54.933 --> 00:07:57.852
His piece about The Beatles
being good because they practiced.

167
00:07:57.853 --> 00:07:59.563
Well. it knocked me on my goddamn ass.

168
00:08:00.147 --> 00:08:01.814
No. I think about it constantly.

169
00:08:01.815 --> 00:08:03.107
- Really?
- Yeah. I'm serious.

170
00:08:03.108 --> 00:08:06.027
- Dad. look who I brought.
- Marisa.

171
00:08:06.028 --> 00:08:07.612
I hope we're not late. Chuck.

172
00:08:07.613 --> 00:08:10.406
We were trying to make you a grandson.

173
00:08:10.407 --> 00:08:13.951
Well. actually. you're not late at all
for a change. dirty dog.

174
00:08:13.952 --> 00:08:15.620
I'm a dirty dog.

175
00:08:15.621 --> 00:08:17.705
- I just love the way sex feels…
- Yeah.

176
00:08:17.706 --> 00:08:18.707
…with my girlfriend.

177
00:08:20.751 --> 00:08:23.252
Very good.

178
00:08:23.253 --> 00:08:25.464
- Please. have a seat. everyone.
- Please. have a seat.

179
00:08:26.381 --> 00:08:28.050
- Thank you for having us. sir.
- Yeah.

180
00:08:33.013 --> 00:08:34.014
Tennis.

181
00:08:34.515 --> 00:08:35.639
Elegance.

182
00:08:35.640 --> 00:08:37.099
Aesthetic perfection.

183
00:08:37.100 --> 00:08:38.893
But tennis isn't just a sport.

184
00:08:38.894 --> 00:08:41.687
She's a living. breathing animal.

185
00:08:41.688 --> 00:08:43.315
and she needs our protection.

186
00:08:46.026 --> 00:08:49.862
An epidemic is sweeping across
our once great nation.

187
00:08:49.863 --> 00:08:52.115
And its name is…

188
00:08:57.120 --> 00:08:58.121
pickleball.

189
00:08:58.956 --> 00:09:02.041
- The novel coronavirus of sports.
- Yeah.

190
00:09:02.042 --> 00:09:05.294
We gave these clowns
Mountain Crest's worst court

191
00:09:05.295 --> 00:09:09.632
as a sort of
hand sanitizer/mask type of deal.

192
00:09:09.633 --> 00:09:12.844
And now these pickleballers
want more courts.

193
00:09:12.845 --> 00:09:15.264
I can't hold off
the expansion vote much longer.

194
00:09:16.306 --> 00:09:19.225
And if we lose. the spread may never stop.

195
00:09:19.226 --> 00:09:22.645
Our club is one of the final strongholds.

196
00:09:22.646 --> 00:09:26.400
We have a responsibility
to become the vaccine

197
00:09:26.942 --> 00:09:30.946
so that someday we can
completely stop talking about them.

198
00:09:31.738 --> 00:09:33.740
Even if they still exist
in similar numbers.

199
00:09:34.992 --> 00:09:36.534
- The end.
- Well…

200
00:09:36.535 --> 00:09:38.036
- Wow.
- That was great. Dad.

201
00:09:38.537 --> 00:09:40.997
The metaphor held up
the whole damn time. Chuck.

202
00:09:40.998 --> 00:09:42.832
But. Chuck.
if these jokers have the numbers.

203
00:09:42.833 --> 00:09:44.375
I mean. what can we even do?

204
00:09:44.376 --> 00:09:48.087
I'll tell you what we can do. Gary.
We can duel.

205
00:09:48.088 --> 00:09:49.547
Like with guns?

206
00:09:49.548 --> 00:09:50.798
Sadly. no.

207
00:09:50.799 --> 00:09:52.176
With tennis rackets.

208
00:09:53.051 --> 00:09:55.220
I made a discovery in the club charter.

209
00:09:55.846 --> 00:09:59.224
We can sidestep the vote
with a duel match.

210
00:09:59.808 --> 00:10:03.769
Each side picks a champion.
and we settle it on the tennis court.

211
00:10:03.770 --> 00:10:05.688
- Well. that's a neat rule.
- Great.

212
00:10:05.689 --> 00:10:08.149
Gosh. what did…
What did they used to duel over?

213
00:10:08.150 --> 00:10:10.818
- Things like this. bylaws and stuff.
- What kinda stuff?

214
00:10:10.819 --> 00:10:11.986
Just stuff.

215
00:10:11.987 --> 00:10:13.571
You know. what…
what's allowed. what isn't.

216
00:10:13.572 --> 00:10:15.031
who can join the club. etcetera.

217
00:10:15.032 --> 00:10:16.574
Who couldn't join before?

218
00:10:16.575 --> 00:10:18.409
I don't know. Kris.

219
00:10:18.410 --> 00:10:21.704
It's an old club.
I don't have a whole list in front of me.

220
00:10:21.705 --> 00:10:25.292
The rule is a good rule.
It's helping us now.

221
00:10:25.834 --> 00:10:27.169
Okay? It's a good rule.

222
00:10:27.669 --> 00:10:29.504
- Just drop it.
- What… Just who couldn't--

223
00:10:29.505 --> 00:10:30.880
I know. But I would just say with my dad…

224
00:10:30.881 --> 00:10:32.674
- Let's eat.
- …just drop it. Let's eat.

225
00:10:35.594 --> 00:10:36.886
- So. all right.
- Great.

226
00:10:36.887 --> 00:10:38.429
Well. let's talk some strategy.

227
00:10:38.430 --> 00:10:40.806
The pickleballers
will put Skip in the duel.

228
00:10:40.807 --> 00:10:42.183
- Oh. God.
- And he used to be

229
00:10:42.184 --> 00:10:44.852
a hell of a tennis player
before he went to the dark side.

230
00:10:44.853 --> 00:10:46.438
So. who do we throw at him?

231
00:10:47.022 --> 00:10:49.774
Well. the club tourney's this weekend.
Maybe we do a little scouting?

232
00:10:49.775 --> 00:10:52.736
Yeah. and whoever wins that
should probably be our guy.

233
00:10:54.154 --> 00:10:55.321
What. is this a joke?

234
00:10:55.322 --> 00:10:56.614
Very funny.

235
00:10:56.615 --> 00:10:58.158
Of course. I'll do it. I'll play.

236
00:10:58.659 --> 00:10:59.951
It isn't gonna be you.

237
00:10:59.952 --> 00:11:03.622
Of course it's gonna be me.
Who else is it gonna be?

238
00:11:05.415 --> 00:11:09.210
Hey. Gary. Would you please tell my dad
that I'm the best player at the club?

239
00:11:09.211 --> 00:11:12.338
Actually. I have to pop into the kitchen
and check on my cobbler.

240
