00:23:10.098 --> 00:23:11.933
- Dusty.
- What? She called me a dink!

486
00:23:11.934 --> 00:23:16.103
Right. The name
of the fricking shot is the dink.

487
00:23:16.104 --> 00:23:18.898
- I know! She called me a dink and I'm--
- She wasn't calling you a dink!

488
00:23:18.899 --> 00:23:21.025
- She just called me a dink!
- She was talking about the shot!

489
00:23:21.026 --> 00:23:24.320
I know. because the shot's called a dink.
That's what I was saying!

490
00:23:24.321 --> 00:23:25.655
Calm down!

491
00:23:25.656 --> 00:23:27.573
- Everybody thinks you're freaking out!
- You calm down.

492
00:23:27.574 --> 00:23:30.409
- Calm down! You're being a sore loser!
- No one thinks I'm freaking out.

493
00:23:30.410 --> 00:23:32.703
- Does anyone think I'm freaking out?
- You're being a sore loser!

494
00:23:32.704 --> 00:23:34.413
- Everybody--
- They're all saying no!

495
00:23:34.414 --> 00:23:35.998
I hate this stupid game!

496
00:23:35.999 --> 00:23:37.251
I'm leaving!

497
00:23:37.918 --> 00:23:39.335
- Hey. kid!
- What?

498
00:23:39.336 --> 00:23:40.670
You want a rematch?

499
00:23:40.671 --> 00:23:42.630
Yes. I'd like that opportunity.

500
00:23:42.631 --> 00:23:44.633
Loser buys lunch!

501
00:23:46.009 --> 00:23:47.010
<i>Gracias.</i>

502
00:23:47.553 --> 00:23:49.220
Boy. when I woke up this morning.

503
00:23:49.221 --> 00:23:54.893
I had no idea that I'd be getting treated
to tacos by the Harry Styles.

504
00:23:55.394 --> 00:23:57.728
- Harry Styles.
- I don't know.

505
00:23:57.729 --> 00:24:02.108
I think he's got
a Chalamet thing going on.

506
00:24:02.109 --> 00:24:03.693
Do you get that all the time?

507
00:24:03.694 --> 00:24:05.444
Do I get Timothée Chalamet?

508
00:24:05.445 --> 00:24:07.030
No. never once in my life.

509
00:24:07.614 --> 00:24:09.574
How do you guys know each other?
What's this group of friends?

510
00:24:09.575 --> 00:24:11.617
Well. I used to be
Gail's personal assistant.

511
00:24:11.618 --> 00:24:15.621
She was a big time lawyer
up until the "incident."

512
00:24:15.622 --> 00:24:17.582
Yeah. it was a misunderstanding.

513
00:24:17.583 --> 00:24:18.666
She punched a cop.

514
00:24:18.667 --> 00:24:21.252
I didn't know he was a cop at the time.

515
00:24:21.253 --> 00:24:22.461
He was wearing a uniform.

516
00:24:22.462 --> 00:24:24.213
Whose side are you on anyway?

517
00:24:24.214 --> 00:24:27.133
The cop's. and I said so at the trial.

518
00:24:27.134 --> 00:24:29.051
You work with them too?

519
00:24:29.052 --> 00:24:31.804
I'm the new kid. Just a pickleball friend.

520
00:24:31.805 --> 00:24:34.307
This is one of the 10.000 hobbies
she took up

521
00:24:34.308 --> 00:24:36.601
after she got divorced and went crazy.

522
00:24:36.602 --> 00:24:38.936
- I did not go crazy! No.
- Yes. you did. Yes. you did.

523
00:24:38.937 --> 00:24:41.439
I experienced
the classic stages of a breakup

524
00:24:41.440 --> 00:24:44.567
that every woman experiences
at some point.

525
00:24:44.568 --> 00:24:46.027
She bought a big. fat snake.

526
00:24:46.028 --> 00:24:48.070
You bought a big. fat snake?

527
00:24:48.071 --> 00:24:50.114
I thought maybe
I could be one of those people

528
00:24:50.115 --> 00:24:52.658
you see with a snake around their neck
at the grocery store.

529
00:24:52.659 --> 00:24:53.951
How'd that work out for ya?

530
00:24:53.952 --> 00:24:55.536
Not good. Not good at all.

531
00:24:55.537 --> 00:24:56.829
Yeah. I'm sure.

532
00:24:56.830 --> 00:24:58.456
- What?
- All right.

533
00:24:58.457 --> 00:25:01.250
You know what? This was really weird.

534
00:25:01.251 --> 00:25:03.211
- but I do… And fun. I had a good time.
- And fun.

535
00:25:03.212 --> 00:25:05.254
Thank you guys for the game.
but I gotta boogie.

536
00:25:05.255 --> 00:25:06.547
- I appreciate ya.
- Hey. Wait.

537
00:25:06.548 --> 00:25:08.883
Actually. could you give me a ride home?

538
00:25:08.884 --> 00:25:10.259
Couldn't your friends do it?

539
00:25:10.260 --> 00:25:11.802
Not me. I walked.

540
00:25:11.803 --> 00:25:12.970
I rode my scooter.

541
00:25:12.971 --> 00:25:14.639
Race you to the Buick.

542
00:25:14.640 --> 00:25:15.890
Okay.

543
00:25:15.891 --> 00:25:17.725
But we have to do this again.

544
00:25:17.726 --> 00:25:21.230
By this. I mean.
you lose and buy us tacos.

545
00:25:23.232 --> 00:25:24.483
Look at that face!

546
00:25:26.109 --> 00:25:27.402
Thank you!

547
00:25:29.363 --> 00:25:31.364
Hey. you should play again.

548
00:25:31.365 --> 00:25:33.783
You could be a great pickleballer.

549
00:25:33.784 --> 00:25:35.993
A great pickleballer? I pass.

550
00:25:35.994 --> 00:25:39.580
Why? Just because the name sucks.
and it looks kind of dorky.

551
00:25:39.581 --> 00:25:43.376
and most people out there are out of shape
and have never played a sport before?

552
00:25:43.377 --> 00:25:45.086
Yes. those are the exact reasons.

553
00:25:45.087 --> 00:25:48.548
But that is why we could dominate. Dusty.

554
00:25:48.549 --> 00:25:51.008
It could be such a bloodbath.

555
00:25:51.009 --> 00:25:54.012
It's just not for me.
It's just a little bit too goofy for me.

556
00:25:54.555 --> 00:25:55.889
Okay. I got it.

557
00:25:57.599 --> 00:26:01.727
Wow. I cannot believe you would
gamble with a machine like this.

558
00:26:01.728 --> 00:26:05.231
- Okay. Okay.
- She's a beauty.

559
00:26:05.232 --> 00:26:07.733
- It's got a cigarette lighter…
- Okay.

560
00:26:07.734 --> 00:26:10.529
- …a tape deck. a manual recline lever.
- Yeah.

561
00:26:12.281 --> 00:26:13.282
Wow!

562
00:26:16.285 --> 00:26:17.368
This is it.

563
00:26:17.369 --> 00:26:18.452
Right here?

564
00:26:18.453 --> 00:26:19.829
- Yep.
- All right.

565
00:26:19.830 --> 00:26:22.123
Anyhoo. thanks for the ride.

566
00:26:22.124 --> 00:26:23.833
Hey. gimme your phone.

567
00:26:23.834 --> 00:26:24.917
For what?

568
00:26:24.918 --> 00:26:25.919
Just gimme.

569
00:26:27.254 --> 00:26:28.338
What are you doing?

570
00:26:29.715 --> 00:26:32.633
Now you have my number
for when you change your mind

571
00:26:32.634 --> 00:26:34.469
and wanna come play pickleball with me.

572
00:26:36.597 --> 00:26:38.431
- Thanks again.
- You got it.

573
00:26:38.432 --> 00:26:41.684
Remember. Dusty. we could dominate.

574
00:26:41.685 --> 00:26:42.686
Bloodbath!

575
00:26:49.693 --> 00:26:53.196
Why did we have to drive 45 minutes
to a sporting goods store?

576
00:26:53.197 --> 00:26:54.906
They have all this stuff at the pro shop.

577
00:26:54.907 --> 00:26:55.990
Well. better selection.

578
00:26:55.991 --> 00:26:58.826
Plus. I feel like we don't get to spend
enough quality time together.

579
00:26:58.827 --> 00:27:00.913
Yeah. I've been thinking that as well.

580
00:27:01.747 --> 00:27:02.748
Here it is.

581
00:27:03.248 --> 00:27:05.417
Look at this. Pickleball.

582
00:27:05.918 --> 00:27:07.544
So stupid.

583
00:27:08.045 --> 00:27:10.671
Yo. imagine if I bought one of these

584
00:27:10.672 --> 00:27:14.175
as like a goof on
the salesperson or whatever.

585
00:27:14.176 --> 00:27:15.927
I don't even know where to laugh.

586
00:27:15.928 --> 00:27:17.595
- Picture this.
- Yeah.

587
00:27:17.596 --> 00:27:21.182
- It's me. but I'm actually buying…
- Yeah.

588
00:27:21.183 --> 00:27:22.266
Good. they have it.

589
00:27:22.267 --> 00:27:27.605
Okay. this paddle right here.
but with a totally straight face.

590
00:27:27.606 --> 00:27:29.065
Okay. I just got it.

591
00:27:29.066 --> 00:27:31.317
It's like kind of
alternative style comedy…

592
00:27:31.318 --> 00:27:33.611
- Yes. Walk up there…
- … like Andy Kaufman.

593
00:27:33.612 --> 00:27:35.738
But I'm gonna actually buy it
and take it home.

594
00:27:35.739 --> 00:27:39.993
So give me. like. literally one second
to see which one's the funniest.

595
00:27:40.744 --> 00:27:42.286
- Yeah. yeah. Okay.
- It's Andy. Andy!

596
00:27:42.287 --> 00:27:44.038
This would be the funniest.
So I'll bet with the total--

597
00:27:44.039 --> 00:27:45.040
Dusty. look.

598
00:27:45.582 --> 00:27:46.875
It's fricking Roddick.

599
00:27:48.043 --> 00:27:49.460
- Andy!
- Hi. Andy.

600
00:27:49.461 --> 00:27:50.962
How are you? Nice to see you.

601
00:27:50.963 --> 00:27:52.631
You know what we should do as a joke?

602
00:27:53.173 --> 00:27:56.927
We should crawl outta here
and sneak out the back.

603
00:27:57.427 --> 00:27:59.428
Joking time's over. Dusty.

604
00:27:59.429 --> 00:28:01.222
- Look at him. acting all cocky.
- Yeah.

605
00:28:01.223 --> 00:28:03.391
- We gotta go rattle his cage. man.
- I would.

606
00:28:03.392 --> 00:28:05.935
You know I would. but we wasted so much
time on your stupid prank thing.

607
00:28:05.936 --> 00:28:07.687
we don't have the time.
We gotta get back to work.

608
00:28:07.688 --> 00:28:11.107
You have to! You're out here doing
groundbreaking guerrilla comedy.

609
00:28:11.108 --> 00:28:14.694
Meanwhile. he's reduced to signing
some random book like a loser.

610
00:28:14.695 --> 00:28:17.738
That's not a random book. it's his book.
He wrote it. That's not--

611
00:28:17.739 --> 00:28:19.574
- But it should be your book. Dusty.
- I agree.

612
00:28:19.575 --> 00:28:21.784
These are your stories. You won the Opens.

613
00:28:21.785 --> 00:28:23.828
Take a breath. Don't get hot.
Don't get… PJ. I know you're…

614
00:28:23.829 --> 00:28:25.247
- Yo. Roddick!
- No!

615
00:28:27.332 --> 00:28:29.751
Andy! Hey. brother.

616
00:28:30.544 --> 00:28:33.129
Dusty. Dusty Boyd. Hammer.

617
00:28:33.130 --> 00:28:35.464
- Oh. yeah. mate. Chuck's son. Yeah.
- Yeah. Chuck's son.

618
00:28:35.465 --> 00:28:38.176
- Yeah. good seeing you. brother.
- Good to see you. It's been a while.

619
00:28:38.177 --> 00:28:40.469
How's your dad doing?
Is… At the same club?

620
00:28:40.470 --> 00:28:42.638
We both are still at the club. actually.

621
00:28:42.639 --> 00:28:44.599
- You work for him?
- No. I work with him.

622
00:28:44.600 --> 00:28:46.184
We kinda co-run the place.

623
00:28:46.185 --> 00:28:48.603
Why does your shirt say.
"Junior Tennis Instructor"?

624
00:28:48.604 --> 00:28:51.522
That didn't exactly sound like
begging for forgiveness. Andy.

625
00:28:51.523 --> 00:28:53.608
- I'd slow down with that.
- You wanna try again?

626
00:28:53.609 --> 00:28:54.859
What's he talking about?

627
00:28:54.860 --> 00:28:57.987
He's talking about
the 2000 Vero Beach Classic.

628
00:28:57.988 --> 00:28:59.364
This pimp had you dead to rights.

629
00:28:59.948 --> 00:29:02.617
2000. I won that year. and who's the pimp?

630
00:29:02.618 --> 00:29:03.910
- He's the pimp!
- Not a pimp.

631
00:29:03.911 --> 00:29:05.578
I'm sorry. I'm so lost.

632
00:29:05.579 --> 00:29:08.956
How'd you slick the floor down?
Grease? Oil?

633
00:29:08.957 --> 00:29:11.043
A third. more sinister option?

634
00:29:12.002 --> 00:29:13.085
I'm so confused.

635
00:29:13.086 --> 00:29:14.921
It's just my friend's getting
a little hot--

636
00:29:14.922 --> 00:29:16.005
You're such a liar.

637
00:29:16.006 --> 00:29:18.299
You kiss Brooklyn Decker
with that lying tongue?

638
00:29:18.300 --> 00:29:21.303
I mean. I do. She loves it.
But I'm not lying.

639
00:29:21.803 --> 00:29:23.721
- Anyways. man. it was good to see you.
- You too. Andy.

640
00:29:23.722 --> 00:29:26.015
- Tell your old man I said hello. Okay.
- Will do. Great to see you. man.

641
00:29:26.016 --> 00:29:27.768
- Congrats on the book. Yeah.
- Cheers. thanks.

642
00:29:29.728 --> 00:29:32.814
Dusty. I've realized that you haven't been
completely honest with me.

643
00:29:34.483 --> 00:29:36.609
Roddick's an even bigger arsehole
than you said.

644
00:29:36.610 --> 00:29:37.611
Yeah.

645
00:29:38.195 --> 00:29:39.570
Yeah. Thanks. Peej.

646
00:29:39.571 --> 00:29:41.656
- I mean. he's totally lying.
- Yeah.

647
00:29:41.657 --> 00:29:43.157
So frustrating. right?

648
00:29:43.158 --> 00:29:44.784
That's annoying as hell.

649
00:29:44.785 --> 00:29:45.786
Agreed.

650
00:30:04.847 --> 00:30:07.265
<i>Two promising young players here.</i>

651
00:30:07.266 --> 00:30:10.351
<i>Boyd has dominated the Juniors
with his powerful serve.</i>

652
00:30:10.352 --> 00:30:12.688
<i>but will that translate here
at the pro level?</i>

653
00:30:13.730 --> 00:30:16.315
{\an8}<i>Wow. sure did not on that point.</i>

654
00:30:16.316 --> 00:30:18.819
<i>but Roddick may have
just gotten lucky with timing.</i>

655
00:30:25.409 --> 00:30:27.785
{\an8}<i>Well. I guess
he didn't get lucky after all.</i>

656
00:30:27.786 --> 00:30:30.038
<i>Roddick just seems to be
a way better tennis player.</i>

657
00:30:32.583 --> 00:30:36.002
{\an8}<i>This is when it's got to be tough
to have your dad as a coach.</i>

658
00:30:36.003 --> 00:30:39.756
<i>It's moments like this that make me glad
I grew up without a father.</i>

659
00:30:43.552 --> 00:30:45.970
<i>Oh. no.</i>

660
00:30:45.971 --> 00:30:49.015
- <i>No. no. no. no. no.</i>
- <i>Go on.</i>

661
00:30:49.016 --> 00:30:51.852
<i>Boyd seems to be running off the court?</i>

662
00:30:52.477 --> 00:30:55.062
<i>Possible there is
some kind of medical issue.</i>

663
00:30:55.063 --> 00:30:59.775
<i>or maybe after all that hype.
the pressure is just too much for him.</i>

664
00:30:59.776 --> 00:31:02.613
<i>That is a tough thing to see in a debut.</i>

665
00:31:16.251 --> 00:31:17.960
All right. match point.

666
00:31:17.961 --> 00:31:18.962
Oh. yes.

667
00:31:20.130 --> 00:31:21.507
I'm gonna get ya.

668
00:31:26.512 --> 00:31:28.387
Still got it! Yes!

669
00:31:28.388 --> 00:31:30.932
Would've been easier to have won that
with a dink. you know?

670
00:31:30.933 --> 00:31:32.725
Never gonna happen. No.

671
00:31:32.726 --> 00:31:34.352
Well. that was easily the best game

672
00:31:34.353 --> 00:31:37.605
against a woman three decades
older than you I've seen you play.

673
00:31:37.606 --> 00:31:38.898
Yeah. easily.

674
00:31:38.899 --> 00:31:42.902
- Yeah! Yes!
- You're so proud of yourself.

675
00:31:42.903 --> 00:31:44.654
Well. I haven't been
getting a lot of wins lately.

676
00:31:44.655 --> 00:31:46.781
- Sad.
- It feels good.

677
00:31:46.782 --> 00:31:48.574
No. I know. Me neither.

678
00:31:48.575 --> 00:31:51.578
- Take 'em where we can get 'em. Cheers.
- Oh. yeah. Hell. yeah.

679
00:31:54.540 --> 00:31:55.623
God.

680
00:31:55.624 --> 00:31:58.125
Eleven missed calls from my ex.

681
00:31:58.126 --> 00:31:59.127
Eleven?

682
00:32:00.295 --> 00:32:02.297
Don't ask. Don't wanna talk about it.

683
00:32:02.798 --> 00:32:03.799
I get it.

684
00:32:04.550 --> 00:32:07.802
There's an event
that we go to together every year.

685
00:32:07.803 --> 00:32:11.139
and he's calling me to ask me
if he can bring his new girlfriend to it.

686
00:32:12.099 --> 00:32:13.307
That bitch.

687
00:32:13.308 --> 00:32:16.102
No. she's actually a really nice person.

688
00:32:16.103 --> 00:32:20.022
- She is? Well. that's great.
- I hate her 50-year-old guts so much.

689
00:32:20.023 --> 00:32:22.775
I'll be honest. I don't know
what you're looking for with this story.

690
00:32:22.776 --> 00:32:25.069
- I know. I know it's confusing.
- Yeah.

691
00:32:25.070 --> 00:32:26.737
Well. here's the thing.

692
00:32:26.738 --> 00:32:31.200
When I left him.
I thought that I was gonna be the winner

693
00:32:31.201 --> 00:32:32.535
- of the divorce.
- Sure.

694
00:32:32.536 --> 00:32:37.123
But now he's parading her all around.
and I'm still single.

695
00:32:37.124 --> 00:32:39.710
- And so I. of course. cannot…
- And that hurts.

696
00:32:40.544 --> 00:32:41.878
…show my face there.

697
00:32:41.879 --> 00:32:43.630
- You're not gonna go.
- No.

698
00:32:44.423 --> 00:32:46.299
- That sucks.
- Yeah.

699
00:32:46.300 --> 00:32:49.468
- But why'd you leave him?
- He was just such a child.

700
00:32:49.469 --> 00:32:51.429
He had no aspirations.

701
00:32:51.430 --> 00:32:55.975
He didn't have many friends.
just one weird friend really.

702
00:32:55.976 --> 00:32:59.770
who just was. "Yes. yes. yes"
to everything he said.

703
00:32:59.771 --> 00:33:01.189
He was sort of a suck-up.

704
00:33:01.190 --> 00:33:06.027
And he was always telling these boring.
boring stories about his glory days.

705
00:33:06.028 --> 00:33:07.695
He doesn't sound so bad.

706
00:33:07.696 --> 00:33:09.447
The truth is.

707
00:33:09.448 --> 00:33:14.119
I would've put up with all that
if he'd ever just shown up for me.

708
00:33:17.539 --> 00:33:18.789
Hey!

709
00:33:18.790 --> 00:33:21.375
You two gonna hog the court
and gab all night

710
00:33:21.376 --> 00:33:23.127
or you looking to run some pickle?

711
00:33:23.128 --> 00:33:24.754
We'll run some pickle!

712
00:33:24.755 --> 00:33:26.423
- Is that okay with you?
- Yeah.

713
00:33:27.049 --> 00:33:28.174
- We'll be partners.
- Yep.

714
00:33:28.175 --> 00:33:31.136
- Let's do it.
- What are they though?

715
00:33:42.397 --> 00:33:43.689
- Yes!
- Uh-huh. uh-huh.

716
00:33:43.690 --> 00:33:45.942
I can't with these two.
I honestly can't do another second.

717
00:33:45.943 --> 00:33:47.944
- Listen. Okay. they're grunters.
- What?

718
00:33:47.945 --> 00:33:50.279
- You think?
- I've played people like this before.

719
00:33:50.280 --> 00:33:53.866
and the only way to beat them
is to out-grunt them.

720
00:33:53.867 --> 00:33:56.494
Or we could beat them
by being better players. which we are.

721
00:33:56.495 --> 00:33:58.871
No. that'll never work.
